THOUGHT: XmlUtilities.read is annotated @Nullable and can return null (e.g., when JAXBContext is null). Tilesets.load currently dereferences tileset without a null-check, causing the NullAway error. The safest fix is to handle the null case locally: if tileset is null, throw a TmxException (similar to other error handling) instead of calling finish. This avoids changing XmlUtilities or other callers and should not introduce new errors. I’ll update Tilesets.load accordingly and then run the Gradle compile to confirm the NullAway error count decreases by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '18,22c\    try {
      Tileset tileset = XmlUtilities.read(Tileset.class, resourceName);
      if (tileset == null) {
        throw new TmxException("Failed to load tileset from URL: " + resourceName);
      }
      tileset.finish(resourceName);
      return tileset;
    } catch (JAXBException e) {
      throw new TmxException(e);
    }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/resources/Tilesets.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log```

